{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following circle graphs best represents the information in the bar graph shown?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the bar graph, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yellow shirts, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> red shirts, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blue shirts, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> green shirt. This means that the number of shirts that were <i>not</i> yellow is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e52388ffea4f0d9c22495e8e8b10f2d12c871d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 2 + 2 = 6 + 2 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"172\" height=\"15\" /> and the total number of shirts is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/232baead1207f7962d526e6375fe2f0828d3fbc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 + 8 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>First, since the number of shirts that weren't yellow was equal to the number of yellow shirts, the number of yellow shirts must be half of the total.\n</p><p>Next, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed7e31e6440011e6998427b97f3552f3180c8c55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{16} = \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" /> of the shirts were red.\n</p><p>Third, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04e60643868f88dfcfd83a0198b9732ef77da599.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{16} = \\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" /> of the shirts were blue. The number of blue and green shirts were equal, so this is also the fraction of the number of shirts that were green\n</p><p>Combining this into a circle graph, the closest answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0f592d678eca8104791846d8140923e313a09ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"41\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we can see that the number of yellow shirts must be half of the total. Of the answer choices, the only one that shows a circle graph with half yellow is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0f592d678eca8104791846d8140923e313a09ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"41\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)